{
  "name": "Text parts",
  "description": "A text layer with parts draws each part in its own colour, weight and size, and each part set to colour by value reads its own band table. The price line takes the layer look for its words, a semibold 21 pt number in its band colour, and a rule aimed at the number makes it bold. The weather line has two numbers with two different band tables, one typed out of order. The car line mixes layer rules and part rules: the layer rule recolours and resizes every part that has no colour or size of its own, a part rule rewrites one part's words, a part rule recolours the number while its band still wins for the digits, a part rule hides the charging part, and a rule aimed at a part id that no part has does nothing. A layer rule that sets the text replaces the parts with that text in the layer look. A countdown ignores parts. A missing entity reads --, an empty part stays empty with no runs, and a part with a table but no colour by value has no runs. When every part is hidden the text is empty and the parts list is empty. Parts are walked by the compiler, so an entity only a part reads is still registered.",
